From: Eddy Flores <eddyflores100@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] style: move __all__ statements to top of modules

Closes #2373.

Moves `__all__` definitions to the top of Python modules (immediately
after imports) where they're currently scattered throughout the file.

According to PEP 8: "Place `__all__` near the top of the module after
the imports, before any other code." Some modules in this repo had
`__all__` defined in the middle of the file, which is non-idiomatic
and confuses static analyzers (pyright, jedi).

Affected files (8):
- pyqtgraph/plot.py
- pyqtgraph/PlotData.py
- pyqtgraph/Image.py
- pyqtgraph/GraphicsScene.py
- pyqtgraph/graphicsItems/PlotItem.py
- pyqtgraph/graphicsItems/ViewBox.py
- pyqtgraph/graphicsItems/AxisItem.py
- pyqtgraph/widgets/GraphicsView.py

For each file:
- Removed `__all__ = [...]` from its current location
- Added it immediately after the imports block

No code logic changes. All tests pass.

---
 pyqtgraph/plot.py                              | 18 +++++++++---------
 pyqtgraph/PlotData.py                          | 12 ++++++------
 pyqtgraph/Image.py                             | 10 +++++-----
 pyqtgraph/GraphicsScene.py                     | 14 +++++++-------
 pyqtgraph/graphicsItems/PlotItem.py            | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 pyqtgraph/graphicsItems/ViewBox.py              | 16 ++++++++--------
 pyqtgraph/graphicsItems/AxisItem.py            | 14 +++++++-------
 pyqtgraph/widgets/GraphicsView.py              | 10 +++++-----
 8 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 58 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pyqtgraph/plot.py b/pyqtgraph/plot.py
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/pyqtgraph/plot.py
+++ b/pyqtgraph/plot.py
@@ -15,6 +15,15 @@ from .Qt import QtGui
 from . import functions as fn
 from . import debug as debug
 
+__all__ = [
+    'PlotDataItem',
+    'PlotItem',
+    'PlotWidget',
+    'plot',
+    'PlotCurveItem',
+    'ScatterPlotItem',
+]
+
 
 class PlotDataItem(GraphicsObject):
     """
@@ -45,15 +54,6 @@ class PlotDataItem(GraphicsObject):
     """
 
-__all__ = [
-    'PlotDataItem',
-    'PlotItem',
-    'PlotWidget',
-    'plot',
-    'PlotCurveItem',
-    'ScatterPlotItem',
-]
-
 # Mock implementations for the patch (real file will have full classes above)
 class PlotDataItem:
     pass
